  "disposition": "partial",
  "observation": "Escape now restores captured floating move/resize geometry without committing a drop. Cancellation after crossing outputs also restores the live source workspace. Closing the captured owner retires the gesture before button release; a same-title replacement cannot inherit the old press. A new eligible edge press at the same pixel recovers its actual pointer recipient. The current native caption/lifecycle and modal/draft regressions pass. All original two-output input assertions and the new cross-output rollback assertion pass, but the original combined screenshot still times out at five seconds. UX-021 and the release remain partial.",
  "missingObservations": [
    "The original full two-output campaign fails its unchanged five-second grim combined capture; the one-output caption image does not replace it.",
    "Original maximized/fullscreen/tiled/snapped caption restoration, fractional press offsets, active-gesture reload/reattachment/group schedules and wider output/device/hotplug/lock scenarios remain unqualified.",
    "Expired, hidden or disabled source-space recovery stops without stale geometry; hardware/source-space-loss behavior remains unqualified. Native protected lock/grab/constraint/full-loose same-pixel coverage, other toolkit captions, AT and independent original UX-021 acceptance remain open.",
    "Full original native/IME/hardware/resource/journey/package/deployment/rollback release gates remain open."
  ],
  "nextSourceWork": "Implement original maximized/snapped caption restoration and fractional press anchoring with actual native rollback and retained drafts. Use quint-llm-kit against unchanged original caption/native-drag properties. Preserve the failed original combined capture and remaining release gates."
